Experiment 12: Design and Implement a Full CI/CD Pipeline Using GitHub Actions

1. Aim

To design and implement a complete Continuous Integration and Continuous Deployment (CI/CD) pipeline using GitHub Actions to automatically test a project, prepare a website for deployment, and deploy it using GitHub Pages.

2. Requirements

1. A GitHub account.
2. An existing GitHub repository.
3. A website written in HTML.
4. A Python program and its test file.
5. GitHub Actions enabled in the repository.
6. GitHub Pages deployment permissions.
7. An internet connection.

Repository URL:

https://github.com/Sudiksha784/My-First-Git-Project

3. Introduction

CI/CD is a software development practice that automates testing, building, and deployment.

Continuous Integration (CI) automatically checks code changes by running tests.

Continuous Delivery/Deployment (CD) prepares the application for release and deploys it to a target environment.

GitHub Actions allows developers to define automated workflows using YAML files stored inside the ".github/workflows/" directory.

In this experiment, the pipeline contains three stages:

1. Test: Run automated Python unit tests.
2. Build: Prepare the website and upload it as a deployment artifact.
3. Deploy: Publish the website using GitHub Pages.

Each stage depends on the successful completion of the previous stage.

